{"ts": 1784362603.3308234, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode -- this was a strongly directional SHORT trade that ran from 0 to +205pts peak (t=44m) and stayed above +150pts through the final frame at +188pts. Every pullback (giveback 20-49%) recovered into a new high within 1-3 frames, and PROPP/HA fires were mostly with-direction at the key junctures, so there was never a genuine wrong-direction signature -- no sustained breakdown below a rising floor, no cascade of against-fires coinciding with a lower low. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that fails to make a new high within a few frames combined with 3/3 fires against as the real bail trigger, rather than treating any single deep giveback (e.g. the 40-49% ones) as reason to exit a trade that's still deeply profitable.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 55}
